<section id="bbs018" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>Two options side by side under a working title, each a subtle box with a label, a title, a short description and a short list of matched length; the recommended option carries the solid label.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="VIMCmMOKDe"><h2>Ways to recover warehouse capacity</h2><grid vertical-sizing="fill" spacing="medium"><grid-item colspan="30" cell-style="subtle" id="-Regzvgz_c"><labels><label variant="solid">Option A</label></labels><h3>Add a second shift</h3><p>Reopen the evening shift at the main warehouse with the existing team plus six hires.</p><ul><li>Capacity back within six weeks</li><li>No new lease or equipment</li><li>Overtime cost until hires start</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item colspan="30" cell-style="subtle" id="fbbyx6LX2A"><labels><label variant="solid">Option B · Recommended</label></labels><h3>Open a regional depot</h3><p>Lease a small depot in the south and move the standing-schedule accounts onto it.</p><ul><li>Shorter routes for the slowest region</li><li>Room for the new lines' stock</li><li>Twelve weeks to first delivery</li></ul></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>